# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4, 7 and 8: the chosen clause's dynamic is the page's `$picked`, so a write of the clause's hold, or of the page's `$tail` it reads, changes the page's label in that tick.
test some_clause

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="more")
    1: Ui.Button(label="some 3")
    2: Ui.Label(text="n3")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="n3!")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="n3!+")

test none_clause

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="more")
    1: Ui.Button(label="none")
    2: Ui.Label(text="zero")

tick 1
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="zero!")
